message: "If you use this software or draft, please cite it as below."
title: "Reliability & Fallback Design Patterns for Multi-Agent LLM Systems"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Ishfaq
    given-names: Muhammad Ashar
    affiliation: "The Islamia University of Bahawalpur"
  - family-names: Ishfaq
    given-names: Muhammad Asad
    affiliation: "Indiana University Bloomington"

abstract: >-
  Controlled comparison of fallback strategies (no fallback, blind retry,
  tool-grounded retry, deterministic checkpointing, graceful degradation,
  cross-agent verification, and one tested P1+P2 composition) in a
  multi-agent multi-hop QA pipeline, measured on pass rate, latency, and
  cost. Targeted patterns beat no-fallback when they address common
  recoverable failure modes; blind retry does not after question-level
  McNemar correction.

keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - large language models
  - reliability
  - fallback
  - LangGraph
  - NeurIPS

